.Dd May 21, 2026
.Dt ORACLED 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm oracled
.Nd Oracle capability-world service manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl p Ar pidfile
.Op Fl T
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the userspace service manager for the Oracle capability world.
It is started by
.Xr rc 8
and is not a replacement for
.Xr init 8 .
.Pp
During startup,
.Nm
daemonizes, writes a pidfile, applies kernel process controls with
.Xr procctl 2 ,
opens
.Pa /dev/cap_rt ,
and waits for events.
It uses
.Xr kqueue 2
to handle signals and child process exits.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-p pidfile"
.It Fl d
Run in the foreground and log to standard error as well as syslog.
.It Fl p Ar pidfile
Write the process ID to
.Ar pidfile
instead of
.Pa /var/run/oracled.pid .
.It Fl T
Test mode.
Run without requiring root, without daemonizing, and without applying
privileged process or capability-runtime setup.
This option is intended for automated tests.
.El
.Sh PROCESS CONTROLS
When not running in test mode,
.Nm
uses
.Xr procctl 2
to:
.Bl -bullet
.It
become a reaper for its future child process subtree;
.It
verify and log reaper status;
.It
mark itself protected from swap-exhaustion kills;
.It
disable tracing and core dumps; and
.It
enable kernel logging for fatal signal exits.
.El
.Pp
These controls do not provide authorization for ordinary signals sent by
privileged users.
Signal authorization and stronger access policy are expected to be provided by
future CAP_RT and MAC policy integration.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/run/oracled.pid"
.It Pa /var/run/oracled.pid
Default pidfile.
.It Pa /dev/cap_rt
CAP_RT control device opened by
.Nm .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kqueue 2 ,
.Xr procctl 2 ,
.Xr cap_rt 4 ,
.Xr rc 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in 5BSD as the initial Oracle userspace service manager.
